# 1. UGREEN Hackathon 2026 on AI NAS

Coordinate: 1.1.1/1.1.1/1.1.2
Organizer / platform: UGREEN (Devpost)
Event: https://ugreenhackathon.devpost.com/
Window: Registration & Round 1: Oct 22 - Nov 15, 2026. Finalist invitations Nov 21, 2026. Round 2: Nov 22-30, 2026 (each finalist gets one assigned testing day, Nov 22-28, on an iDX6011 Pro, 64GB). Winners announced ~Dec 6, 2026.
Official deadline: Round 1 closes Nov 15, 2026, 11:45 PM PT. Round 2 closes Nov 30, 2026, 11:45 PM PT.
Internal target: Round 1 submit-ready by Nov 13, 2026 (official close minus 2 days).
Prize: $46,000 total: Gold $20,000 / Silver $10,000 / Bronze $6,000 / Most Creative $5,000 x2. One prize per project.
Eligibility: Individuals and teams of up to 3, age of majority. Existing organizations are NOT eligible. US eligible (Quebec excluded); the rules' country list excludes India, China, Brazil, Russia, Ukraine and others.
AI tools: Disclosure required: SKILL.md or its references must disclose the AI tools used and their principal uses, third-party components with sources and licenses, and the principal functionality developed for the hackathon.
Submission: Round 1: (1) a PDF (<=1 MB) answering ten specified questions, <=500 English words total across the ten responses; (2) a Skill Package ZIP (<=10 MB, <=1 MB per file, <=100 files) containing SKILL.md. Skills must follow the Uliya Skill Development Standard and use supported UGOS CLI capabilities through registered expert agents - custom executables, scripts and binaries are PROHIBITED in the package. Judging, equal weights: User Value, Innovation & Differentiation, Technical Quality, AI NAS Fit & Validation.
Status: round 1 drafted
Verification: Verified from the official rules and event page fetched 2026-11-10; these facts supersede the research report's index notes where they differ (the PDF is a ten-question form, not a free-form proposal).

Notes:
- Our entry: 'Phext Memory' - a personal-memory skill: the owner's corpus as phext plain text on their own NAS, four operations (read / write / search / navigate) exposed via UGOS capabilities; the existing phext MCP server is disclosed as prior reference work, not a package component.
- Current artifact: round-1 draft at ~/workspace/hackathon-campaign/ugreen/ (proposal.md + SKILL.md; the ten responses total 476 words).
- New-work rule: the Skill and its core workflow must be newly developed during the hackathon; pre-conceived ideas and prior components are allowed with disclosure. Hold that line in all later materials.
- Open item: the phext license-name placeholder in SKILL.md ('as published with the format's source') must be confirmed from the phext repo before the package is finalized.
- Open technical question: whether UGOS exposes skills to external MCP clients is not verified; it needs the Starter Kit docs (ai.ugreen.com/pages/hackathon-starter-kit).
