Submission: Working demo app; public GitHub/GitLab repo with an open-source license showing Firebase AI Logic actually being called; demo video <=3 min (YouTube, English or English subtitles); text description. Hard constraint: all app AI inference must go through Firebase AI Logic (on-device + cloud hybrid); direct calls to other model APIs are not allowed.
Status: not started
Verification: Dates, theme and AI-tool stance read on the event's own Devpost page (index fetch, 2026-11-11). The Devpost rules page said 'Official Rules are not yet available' at fetch time - re-check the rules before building.
# 3. The Gemma 4 Developer Agent Competition

Coordinate: 1.1.1/1.1.1/1.1.4
Organizer / platform: Google DeepMind (Kaggle)
Event: https://www.kaggle.com/competitions/gemma-4-developer-agent
Window: Paper Track closes Nov 12, 2026. Entry / rules-acceptance deadline Nov 25, 2026. Final submission Dec 2, 2026, 23:59 UTC.
Official deadline: Final submission Dec 2, 2026, 11:59 PM UTC.
Internal target: Submit-ready by Nov 30, 2026 (official close minus 2 days); the entry plan freezes final candidates Nov 29, 2026.
Prize: $110,000 total, confirmed on Kaggle's own page: main track $65,000 (1st $37,000 / 2nd $18,000 / 3rd $10,000), Paper Track $35,000, Small Model Development bonus $10,000 (best entry built on Gemma 4 E2B/E4B; LoRA allowed). The $75,000 figure in early coverage was a stale header and is dropped.
Eligibility: Teams up to 5; 18+ / age of majority; worldwide except sanctioned regions.
AI tools: The entry IS a post-trained model agent: post-train an open Gemma 4 model into an offline coding agent that fixes Python bugs. LoRA fine-tuning is allowed.
Submission: A declarative-YAML ADK agent package (submission.zip, optional LoRA adapters) - NOT a Kaggle notebook. Evaluation runs on Kaggle's harness: the agent works in an air-gapped sandbox, its patch is extracted and verified SWE-bench-style; metric is Resolution Rate.
Status: entry plan complete
Verification: Prize total and the Nov 25 / Dec 2 dates corroborated on Kaggle's own pages, 2026-11-10 evening (this supersedes the research report's dagger flags for this contest). Still unverified: per-task caps and the 3 GiB zip cap rest on secondary sources quoting the harness README - resolving them is the entry plan's first action.

Notes:
- Entry plan: ~/workspace/hackathon-campaign/gemma4/PLAN.md - Slot A: E4B + LoRA; Slot B: 31B QAT; finals freeze Nov 29, 2026.
- Paper Track (separate line): closes Nov 12, 2026 - closes before campaign start; Hail Mary only. Status: not pursued unless a submittable write-up already exists.
